--TEST--
`Core\Budget`'s three readings agree at every point in a request — held never exceeds the peak, before a spike, while it is held and after it is released — asserted by counting rather than read off a line — `rule:observability/memory-is-three-numbers-on-core-budget`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The invariant, swept rather than sampled. A member that answered plausibly
// at one point — a peak that is `memoryHeld` under another name, say — still
// looks right on its own line, and parts from the held figure only once the
// two are asked at a moment where they must differ. So the same question is
// put three times across a request's shape and the *count* is what is printed.
uint $agreements = 0;

if (Core\Budget::memoryHeld() <= Core\Budget::memoryPeak()) {
    $agreements = $agreements + 1;
}

string $spike = Core\Str::repeat("z", 1048576);
if (Core\Budget::memoryHeld() <= Core\Budget::memoryPeak()) {
    $agreements = $agreements + 1;
}

$spike = "";
if (Core\Budget::memoryHeld() <= Core\Budget::memoryPeak()) {
    $agreements = $agreements + 1;
}

echo "held is never above the peak: ", ($agreements as string), " of 3\n";

// And the peak itself only ever climbs, over the same three points — the other
// half of one mark: a figure that fell back at any of them would be a second
// reading of the current balance wearing the peak's name.
uint $climbs = 0;
uint $mark = Core\Budget::memoryPeak();

string $again = Core\Str::repeat("z", 1048576);
if (Core\Budget::memoryPeak() >= $mark) {
    $climbs = $climbs + 1;
}
$mark = Core\Budget::memoryPeak();

$again = "";
if (Core\Budget::memoryPeak() >= $mark) {
    $climbs = $climbs + 1;
}

echo "the peak never falls: ", ($climbs as string), " of 2\n";

// The third member joins the same sweep, because the trio is only usable if
// all three are one accounting: a request that is still running is inside the
// ceiling it is measured against, at every point it can be asked. A ceiling
// answering `0` is a request under none, which the same condition covers
// rather than needing a second reading to detect.
uint $inside = 0;
uint $ceiling = Core\Budget::memoryLimit();
if ($ceiling == 0 || Core\Budget::memoryHeld() <= $ceiling) {
    $inside = $inside + 1;
}
if ($ceiling == 0 || Core\Budget::memoryPeak() <= $ceiling) {
    $inside = $inside + 1;
}
echo "both readings are inside the ceiling: ", ($inside as string), " of 2\n";
--EXPECT--
held is never above the peak: 3 of 3
the peak never falls: 2 of 2
both readings are inside the ceiling: 2 of 2
